The optional assistant downloads llama.cpp (MIT licence,
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) and language model files from Hugging
Face at the user's request. They are not part of Kontor and come under their
own licences.

At the user's request Kontor downloads a build of CPython (Python Software
Foundation License 2; built by python-build-standalone,
https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone) to run in. It is not
part of Kontor and comes under its own licences, which lie in its folder.

The balance sheet in today's purchasing power uses the consumer price index
for Germany (Verbraucherpreisindex, 2020 = 100): source Statistisches
Bundesamt (Destatis), GENESIS-Online table 61111-0002, Datenlizenz
Deutschland - Namensnennung - Version 2.0 (dl-de/by-2-0,
https://www.govdata.de/dl-de/by-2-0); shipped in price_index.py and, newer
months, fetched from the time series of the Deutsche Bundesbank (series
BBDP1.M.DE.N.VPI.C.A00000.I20.A; source: Deutsche Bundesbank). The figures
in today's money are Kontor's own calculation from it.

Kontor names everything of this kind it uses on a Mac, with version, licence
and origin, under Settings -> Updates.
